[2026-05-29 23:08:33] [agentic_pipeline.py (367)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 3898256] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are an AI agent that makes optimal decisions to win in the game of tic-tac-toe.user\nGAME RULES:\n1. Tic-tac-toe is a two-player board game played on a three-by-three grid. The grid is 0-indexed, where (0,0) is the top-left corner and (2,2) is the bottom-right corner.\n2. Two players take turns placing their marks X and O in empty cells of the grid.\n3. The player who first places three of their marks in a horizontal, vertical, or diagonal line wins.\n4. If all cells are filled and no player wins, the game ends in a draw.\n\nPLAYER INFORMATION:\n1. Your mark is X. You are competing with another player controlling the mark O.\n2. In each of your turns:\n   a. The game state demonstrates the current board with a three-line text grid, where 'X' and 'O' are the marks of the two players, and '_' represents empty cells.\n   b. You need to chose an action to place your mark in an empty cell, based on the given game state and the history of your decisions.\n   c. All legal actions for the current turn are provided in the format of `<X({row},{column})>`, where `X` is your mark, and {row} and {column} are integers indicating the row and column of the cell to place your mark.\n\nRESPONSE INSTRUCTIONS:\nAlways choose only one action from the legal actions and output `<answer>{your chosen action}</answer>` with no extra text after you finish the thinking process. For example, `<answer><X(0,0)></answer>`. Strictly follow the above format and keep your thinking process concise. Responses that do not follow the format will result in immediate loss of the game.\n\nInformation of Turn-1:\n\nThis is your turn. The game state and legal actions for this turn are provided below. Please choose your action and strictly follow the given output format in the response instructions.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n___\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<X(0,0)>, <X(0,1)>, <X(0,2)>, <X(1,0)>, <X(1,1)>, <X(1,2)>, <X(2,0)>, <X(2,1)>, <X(2,2)>.\n\nassistant\n", "response": "<think>\nOkay, let's start by thinking about the best first move in tic-tac-toe. Since the board is empty, I need to choose a position that gives me the best chance to win. The middle position (1,1) is often considered the best because it's part of multiple lines: the middle row, middle column, and both diagonals. So, by taking the center, I can potentially create multiple opportunities to win. Alternatively, corner positions are also good because they are part of two lines each. But the center is more strategic. Let me go with the center. So the action would be X(1,1).\n</think>\n\n<answer><X(1,1)></answer>user\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>, <O(2,2)>.\n\n", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\nOkay, let's start by thinking about the best first move in tic-tac-toe. Since the board is empty, I need to choose a position that gives me the best chance to win. The middle position (1,1) is often considered the best because it's part of multiple lines: the middle row, middle column, and both diagonals. So, by taking the center, I can potentially create multiple opportunities to win. Alternatively, corner positions are also good because they are part of two lines each. But the center is more strategic. Let me go with the center. So the action would be X(1,1).\n</think>\n\n<answer><X(1,1)></answer><|im_end|><|im_start|>user\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>, <O(2,2)>