 and column of the cell to place your mark.\n\nRESPONSE INSTRUCTIONS:\nAlways choose only one action from the legal actions and output `<answer>{your chosen action}</answer>` with no extra text after you finish the thinking process. For example, `<answer><O(0,0)></answer>`. Strictly follow the above format and keep your thinking process concise. Responses that do not follow the format will result in immediate loss of the game.\n\nInformation of Turn-1:\n\nThis is the other player's turn. The game state, legal actions, as well as the chosen action of the other player for this turn are provided below.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n___\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<X(0,0)>, <X(0,1)>, <X(0,2)>, <X(1,0)>, <X(1,1)>, <X(1,2)>, <X(2,0)>, <X(2,1)>, <X(2,2)>.\n\nCHOSEN ACTION:\n<X(1,1)>\nInformation of Turn-2:\n\nThis is your turn. The game state and legal actions for this turn are provided below. Please choose your action and strictly follow the given output format in the response instructions.\n\nGAME STATE:\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nLEGAL ACTIONS:\n<O(0,0)>, <O(0,1)>, <O(0,2)>, <O(1,0)>, <O(1,2)>, <O(2,0)>, <O(2,1)>, <O(2,2)>.\n\nassistant\n", "response": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The game is tic-tac-toe, and I'm playing as O. The previous turn was the other player's (X) turn, and they chose the center (1,1). So the current board state is:\n\n___\n_X_\n___\n\nSo the second row, middle column is X. Now it's my turn to place an O. The legal actions are all the empty cells except (1,1) which is already taken by X.\n\nI need to choose a move that's optimal. Let me think about possible strategies. Since X went for the center, maybe they're trying to create a winning line. But since I'm O, I need to block them or set up my own lines.\n\nLooking at the board, the first row is all empty. The second row has an X in the middle. The third row is empty. The columns: first column is empty, second column has X in the middle, third column is empty.\n\nPossible moves: I need to place O in one of the remaining